Stock validation: on add/update, check product.stock >= desired quantity. But stock isn't decremented until checkout (real systems reserve at checkout). For checkout: re-check stock for all items, emit order confirmed. I won't decrement catalog stock in this demo (catalog read-only) — actually let me decrement? That mutates catalog; fine in-memory but interface ProductCatalog lacks decrement. I'll add `decrementStock(productId, qty)` to catalog port for checkout. Hmm, scope. It's realistic and easy: in-memory catalog decrements atomically, throws InsufficientStockError. I'll do it — shows scalability thinking (inventory at checkout). Actually reserving inventory at checkout within same process is fine.

